{{/* Runs ONCE, at `chezmoi init`. Writes ~/.config/chezmoi/chezmoi.toml on their machine —
     never in this repo. Their answers survive every later `chezmoi update`.

     THIS FILE IS THE QUESTION COUNT. In v1 the rule "three things are theirs to decide" was a
     paragraph asking an agent to count correctly; here it is the length of a list you can read.
     Adding a prompt here is the regression — do it deliberately or not at all.

     TWO questions, both of which cost them a decision rather than a password:

       ccc_mode — the one genuinely personal call. Shipping skip-permissions without asking is
                  what made the site's copy wrong once already; deciding it FOR them is the bug.
       admin    — gates everything that needs sudo later (brew, apt, chsh). Asked once, here,
                  so no later step has to ask again.

     The model question is GONE. Opus is the default because it was already decided on
     2026-08-11 after testing on sonnet ("it was not working really well"). A question whose
     recommended answer is fixed, and whose wrong answer quietly degrades the product, is not a
     decision — it is a trap with a default. Sonnet is mentioned on the page they keep, as the
     way to stretch the allowance. */}}

{{- $cccMode := promptChoiceOnce . "ccc_mode" "Should I ask before every command? (fast = no, careful = yes)" (list "fast" "careful") "fast" -}}
{{- $admin   := promptBoolOnce   . "admin"    "Can I use admin (your password) on this computer when something needs installing?" true -}}

sourceDir = "{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/projects/mwk-genie"

[data]
    ccc_mode = {{ $cccMode | quote }}
    admin    = {{ $admin }}
